Z||000000||tsmagnum1||06-05-2001||10:02 AM||||Could someone give me an idea of what the cost and feasibility of converting an auto. into a 5-speed?(example: cost of a 5-speed tranny and the approx. cost of labor if I choose not to tackle this myself.) The car is a Fiero but has been used as a donor for a Ferrari GTB. The engine is a stock 2.8 V-6. Thanks!!||||reg||11
Z||000001||Will||06-05-2001||07:04 PM||||That's been discussed on several occasions.<BR>There may not be any topics on that left in the active forum.<P>Search both the active tech forum and the tech archives.||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||06-05-2001||08:19 PM||||You better want the conversion pretty bad, 'cause it'll cost ya. <P>The tranny: Isuzu $150<BR>            Getrag $300<P>cable set w/shifter: $100+<P>Flywheel and clutch set w/o core: $250<P>Clutch pedal assy: $50<P>Clutch master, lines, and slave: $200<P>Installation: $500-$1,000<P><BR>The very cheapest it'll be is $1,250 and that's if all goes well, which of course, it won't. I had a real clean 84 that I was going to switch to a 5sp, but didn't when I realized it would cost me about $1000. I would stick with what I have or buy a new donor car.||||reg||1
